Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-30-2001||11:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by edbone:<BR><B>I have an 87 GT with 50K miles on it and just recentlly Its been shaking or vibrating while I accelerate. Any ideas? thanks Eddie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Ed!<BR>Check your rear wheel bearings and CV joints...<BR>At 50K they should be alright, but you never know...<P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||10-31-2001||09:50 AM||||In addition to Crash's checks, check that the mounts are in good shape and that the motor isn't mis-aligned either sitting idle or accelerating. GL<P>EDITED for typos<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
